ndependent polling showing Nelson within single digits, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Representative Stephanie Bice seeks reelection in Oklahoma's 5th District, an Oklahoma City-area seat that leans Republican by nine points. She faces Jena Nelson, a Democrat and educator, along with two independents. Bice holds a decisive financial advantage, having raised $2.4 million and retaining $1.7 million on hand, while Nelson has raised about $739,000 with limited cash remaining.\n\nRatings outlets overwhelmingly place the race in Solid or Safe Republican territory, though a few call it Likely Republican. A Democratic-sponsored September poll showed Bice ahead by five points, and prediction markets give Nelson roughly a 15 percent chance. National Democrats have added the seat to their target list and are investing in the race, a rare move in Oklahoma, and Bice has declined debates so far. The fundamentals still favor Bice clearly, with the main question being the size of her winning margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0816, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07"